        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Finance a treadmill only on terms you fully understand.</strong>
            A true 0% plan, paid off early and automatically, on a machine you would have bought
            with cash, costs nothing extra. Deferred interest, long high-APR terms and subscription
            bundles can cost hundreds of dollars more than the price tag suggests.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Compare the <strong class="text-white">total of all payments</strong> with the best cash
            price, not the monthly figure. If the machine is only affordable on expensive credit,
            a cheaper tier, a used machine or
            <a href="/best-time-of-year-to-buy-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">waiting for a sale</a>
            is usually the better plan.
          </p>
